Take Tcl_EvalFile from Tcl16's DOS layer (src/source.c; docs/DESIGN.md,
sections 4 and 6).

Tiny Tcl's Tcl_EvalFile, which "source" calls, read the script in binary
mode, so a script in DOS text failed: a backslash before CR LF did not
continue the line, a quoted value spanning lines kept the CR, and a ^Z at
the end ran as a command (tests/tinytcl/crlf.tcl, ctrlz.tcl). Its
fallback for a script too large to read whole, Tcl_SmallFootprintEvalFile,
read lines of at most 254 bytes with fgets in text mode and handed each
piece to Tcl_AssembleCmd, kept evaluating after "return", and returned an
uninitialised result for an empty script. Both are removed here; Tcl16's
own Tcl_EvalFile reads DOS text either way.

diff -ru a/tcldosut.c b/tcldosut.c
--- a/tcldosut.c
+++ b/tcldosut.c
@@ -23,199 +23,11 @@
 
 
